uster (10.5.29/galera-26.4.22) across node1/node2/node3 on AlmaLinux 9 (no MariaDB was pre-installed), loaded application data (appdb.orders), took the entire cluster down for a maintenance window, brought it back with all committed writes intact and all three members serving, then performed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on every node, proving changed boot identity and full cluster recovery (3/3 Synced, data intact) after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed mariadb-server, mariadb-server-galera, galera on node1/node2/node3\",\"Configured /etc/my.cnf.d/galera.cnf per node with correct wsrep_provider path (/usr/lib64/galera/libgalera_smm.so) after fixing an initial wrong path\",\"Opened firewalld ports 3306/4444/4567(tcp+udp)/4568 on all nodes\",\"Bootstrapped Galera cluster on node1 via galera_new_cluster\",\"Created appdb.orders table, appuser and sstuser accounts with generated random passwords (kept out of command literals/report)\",\"Started mariadb on node2 and node3, confirmed SST join and wsrep_cluster_size=3, Synced on all nodes\",\"Inserted baseline rows on node1 and a cross-node write on node3, verified replication to node1\",\"Captured pre-maintenance boot_id baseline on all 3 nodes\",\"Stopped mariadb on node3, node2, then node1 (full cluster shutdown for maintenance window), verified node1 retained safe_to_bootstrap:1 with highest seqno\",\"Brought cluster back: bootstrapped node1 via galera_new_cluster, started node2 and node3, verified 3/3 Synced and all 4 committed rows present on every node\",\"Restarted node3, node2, node1 one at a time via systemctl reboot (quorum preserved each time), polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, confirmed mariadb active with wsrep_cluster_size=3, Synced, and all data intact after each restart\",\"Final cross-node verification of cluster size, sync state, and row count on all three nodes\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"3-node Galera cluster established with application data\"